Dev Magic - WordPress Local Development Environment Tool

This tool is designed to help developers quickly set up local WordPress 
development environments with the following features:

- SSL certificate generation with custom Certificate Authority
- Automated Apache virtual host configuration
- Complete WordPress installation and setup
- Database import functionality for existing WordPress sites
- Git project cloning for themes and plugins
- Interactive wizard mode for guided setup
- WordPress site cleanup and removal functionality
- Modular architecture for maintainability

For more information, documentation, and support:
- GitHub: https://github.com/PetyoLazarov92/devmagic
- Issues: https://github.com/PetyoLazarov92/devmagic/issues
- Documentation: See README.md

Coding Standards Compliance:
Shell scripts follow standard bash scripting best practices.

Third-party Dependencies:
This software may interact with or depend on:
- WordPress (GPL v2 or later)
- Apache HTTP Server (Apache License 2.0)
- MySQL/MariaDB (GPL)
- PHP (PHP License)
- OpenSSL (Apache-style license)
- Git (GPL v2)

Users are responsible for ensuring compliance with all applicable licenses
when using this software in conjunction with third-party components.

Disclaimer:
This tool is intended for development environments only. Do not use the
default passwords or certificates generated by this tool in production
environments. Always follow security best practices when deploying
WordPress sites to production.
